    <div class="">
      <p>
        This year in London for the 49th edition, the conference focusses on accessiblity and
        inclusion to encourage as many researchers as possible to attend and share their work as a
        talk or poster, no matter how early-stage it is. Submissions are not assessed or excluded on
        quality grounds, all submissions related to the listed topics are accepted and encouraged.
      </p>
      <p>
        As a conference aimed at PhD students, there is also an industry flavour to the conference
        and we look forward to welcoming industry partners who will also present featured talks at
        the conference and be available to interact with other delegates. Specific sponsors and
        featured talks to be released soon!
      </p>
    </div> -->
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-label={t('about.ledgerLabel')}>
    <div class="about-ledger">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Past</h3>
        <p>
          We will have a focus on how the progress of statistics and probability theory as a field
          over the last fifty years; how it has changed and evolved as mathematics and technology
          have developped.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Present</h3>
        <p>
          We will look to showcase present work: discussion of open theoretical problems, new
          techniques for applied questions along with fresh implementations for industrial problems.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Future</h3>
        <p>
          This conference is an opportunity for students to make new connections with their peers,
          develop experience presenting work in the field and build themselves as the future leaders
          in academia and industry.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">For 2027</p>
      <h2>The Committee.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose prose-stack">
      <p>
        This year the committee is composed of the following PhD students from Imperial College
        London:
      </p>
      <ul class="organiser-list">
        {ORGANISERS.map((name) => <li>{name}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">For 2028</p>
      <h3>The next committee!</h3>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>
        Each year a new university will host the RSC which mean that a new group of students will be
        needed to help organise the conference. Our fifty years of history means we have established
        relationships with universities and sponsors across the UK. This makes organising a great
        opportunity.

        <!-- RSC has thrived on passing from university to university through PhD students for nearly half a century. The established presence with sponsors and universities across the UK makes it a relatively straightforward conference to organise with access to a wealth of historical resources - and something that looks great on a CV for when you complete your PhD. -->
      </p>
      <p>Interested in hosting the 51th RSC? Get in contact with us about hosting for 2028.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

